There is no no-reuse control in that sitting and a no-reuse workspace differs, so it is not comparable to
anything here; it is disclosed because the default container has read 15.7-16.2 ms in other sittings, which, if
comparable, would point against the prediction.

Method: scripts/research-lowlevel.sh --npu --wait-clear 30, tools/bench_dispatch_ab.py
  --pair box=ctl,box --pair path=ctl,boxplain --rounds 4 --iters 300; real and all-NOP each round, order
reversed on even rounds. Requires timing_eligible: true and no foreign contention, else the sitting is void.

Predictions (test minus control, mean of 4 rounds):
  path (boxplain - ctl): same task count, one extra configure; |delta| < 0.15 ms real and NOP.
  box (box - ctl), PER-TASK model (task issue is the cost; the probe's measured ratio applies to the 1,442 tasks
    removed, 1.58 ms NOP, less 26 extra configures estimated at 0.4-0.5 ms):
      NOP  -0.6 to -1.4 ms;  real  -0.4 to -1.1 ms (57-92% of NOP savings reached real dispatch in the
      issue-inject data).
  box, PER-OP model (every instruction op costs alike): +1,806 ops makes box SLOWER: delta > 0.
  The sitting discriminates: a NOP delta below -0.3 ms favours per-task over per-op; above 0 favours per-op.

Verdict (on REAL dispatch, box pair):
  KEEP (land behind the off-by-default flag; default flip is a later block): mean delta <= -0.30 ms AND box lower
    in >= 3/4 rounds.
  KILL: mean delta >= 0, or box lower in <= 1/4 rounds.
  Anything else: INCONCLUSIVE (lands behind the flag, recorded as such).
  If path pair's real delta is > +0.15 ms, the write-up states the path's own cost and the box delta net of it,
  but the verdict above stays on the box pair as registered.
A hang or any mismatch voids the sitting ("control unproven"), no workaround.
